DESCRIPTION:Abstract\n\nPer- and polyfluoroalkyl substances (PFAS) are con
 taminants that have accumulated extensively in soils\, which can act as lo
 ng-term sources of groundwater contamination. Quantifying soil PFAS leachi
 ng is therefore critical for risk assessment\, remediation\, and regulator
 y decision-making. However\, PFAS transport differs fundamentally from tha
 t of conventional contaminants because many PFAS are surfactants that adso
 rb at air–water and solid–water interfaces\, leading to complex retent
 ion b\n\nAges: All ages\nLast synced: 2026-11-09 14:54 PST
LOCATION:Green Earth Sciences Building
