SUMMARY:[Wu Tsai Neurosciences Institute / Stanford Institute for Human-Ce
 ntered Artificial Intelligence (HAI)] Daniel Wurgaft | A Resource Rational
  Analysis of Representations: Geometry\, Inference\, Capacity
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261109T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261109T173000
DTSTAMP:20261109T225406Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-54047808526630-54047808526631@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Abstract\n\nNeural systems process information by forming repr
 esentations of the world. Studies of representational geometry have reveal
 ed remarkably structured representations in biological and artificial syst
 ems\, as well as surprising alignment in representations across systems. W
 hy do representations across systems converge to similar structures\, how 
 do these structures encode concepts and uncertainty over them\, and how ar
 e they shaped by resource constraints?\n\nHere\, we tackle these questions
  i\n\nAges: All ages\nSource: https://neuroscience.stanford.edu/events/sem
 inar-series-wu-tsai-neuro/center-neural-data-science-seminar-series\nLast 
